ProsperoSunshine: hide apps from devices the operator doesn't trust

The PS5 host lists the console's games and homebrew apps, and some of them can change the console: a store can install,
update or uninstall titles. The operator can hide apps from paired devices they don't trust (issue 36). A hidden app is
left out of /applist for such a device, and as a client may start an app by an ID it kept from an earlier list, /launch
refuses it too, as does /resume while one runs. The PS5 code decides (proc::app_allowed, process_ps5.cpp); "PS5 Screen"
is never hidden.

